=== PARITY (web source reproduced end-to-end) ===
  - Data sources (web useLocation + useTranslation): bound through the P1/S8 seam
    BottomTabLocationSource -> BottomTabModel (web `useLocation`) and the P1/S10
    BottomTabStrings facade (web `useTranslation`). No router/navigation state is read
    directly in the view; a tap forwards to the host via BottomTabNavigationSink
    (web `<PrefetchLink to={tab.path}>`).
  - Composition (web `TABS.map`): the static 5-tab catalog is reproduced verbatim and
    in order — Dashboard(/) -> Drives(/drives) -> Charging(/charging) -> Battery(/battery)
    -> Map(/live). Each web lucide glyph maps to its SF Symbol (Home->house.fill,
    Car->car.fill, BatteryCharging->bolt.batteryblock.fill, HeartPulse->waveform.path.ecg,
    MapPin->mappin.and.ellipse). Active tint = brand accent (web `--theme-primary`) +
    icon glow (web `drop-shadow`) + underline indicator (web active `<span>`); inactive =
    text-muted (web `--text-muted`). Chrome = TSMaterial.chrome (.bar) + a hairline top
    border (web `bg-[var(--surface-overlay)] backdrop-blur-xl border-t`).
  - States (the ONLY conditional branch in the web source is `isActive`; the bar is
    static navigation chrome with NO data fetch, so the generic data-states
    loading/empty/error/stale/offline are N/A — not fabricated). The real, reproduced
    states are: ACTIVE (exact tab route), INACTIVE (other tabs), NESTED (a child route
    keeps its parent tab active, web `startsWith(path + '/')`), and NONE-ACTIVE (an
    off-tab route like /settings lights no tab). The surface ALWAYS renders all five
    tabs — it never hides a destination (honors "no hidden surfaces"). Each state has a
    #if DEBUG preview AND an executed unit test.
  - i18n (P1/S10): web keys preserved verbatim — nav.quickNav (container aria-label) +
    nav.dashboard/nav.drives/nav.charging/nav.battery/nav.liveMap (the web `TABS[].i18nKey`
    with their `fallback`: Home/Drives/Charging/Battery/Map). Every code-referenced key is
    declared in BottomTabBar.strings; NO English string literals in native code (all via
    the BottomTabStrings facade + Text(verbatim:)). referenced==declared verified.
  - Accessibility: the nav container carries the VoiceOver label (web `nav aria-label`);
    every tab is a Button with its localized label + the .isSelected trait when active
    (web `aria-current="page"`); 44pt minimum hit target (web `min-w-[48px] min-h-[44px]`);
    Dynamic-Type system fonts (Font.TS) + minimumScaleFactor; reduce-motion honored
    (TSFadeIn + the selection animation via TSAnimation.standard(reduceMotion:)).
  - Telemetry (P1/S11): BottomTabModel.start() emits view.opened with surface slug
    "BottomTabBar" exactly once (OSLogBottomTabTelemetry default; prod app injects the
    shared diagnostics adapter). Re-armed by stop() for a later re-appearance.
  - Placement note (web `lg:hidden`): the bar is compact-width chrome; the host shows it
    only on iPhone and anchors it to the bottom safe area via `.safeAreaInset(edge:.bottom)`.
    The surface itself always renders (no hidden surface); placement is the host's concern,
    matching how the web hides it at the `lg` breakpoint rather than conditionally rendering.

